enged us to get to the moon and back."}),(0,d.jsx)("p",{children:"NASA contractors could make rapid technical advances because the government had been investing in basic research like physics, computer science, and materials science. We had great public schools where a generation of students learned the skills that would create the next wave of inventions. We had world-class universities and welcomed talented people from everywhere."})]}),SECTION_3:(0,d.jsxs)(d.Fragment,{children:[(0,d.jsx)("p",{children:"I was 13 years old when Neil Armstrong took his first steps on the moon, too young to take part myself. But I’ve been lucky enough to be part of more recent dramatic changes driven by innovation."}),(0,d.jsx)("p",{children:"One is the digital revolution, starting with the creation of the personal computer and the software that would run it. When Paul Allen and I founded Microsoft, we were able to draw on talent from great universities and an ecosystem that made it possible to challenge entrenched competitors. It was a huge benefit to us to be in the U.S."})]}),SECTION_4:(0,d.jsxs)(d.Fragment,{children:[(0,d.jsxs)("p",{children:["Another revolution is the one taking places in"," ",(0,d.jsx)("a",{href:"https://www.breakthroughenergy.org/",children:"energy"}),"; it’s leading to new sources that are cleaner, better, and cheaper than what we have today. And there is the"," ",(0,d.jsx)("a",{href:"https://www.gatesfoundation.org/our-work/areas-of-impact/health",children:"global health"})," ","revolution, which has seen the invention of new vaccines, new ways to distribute them, and lifesaving treatments for deadly diseases like AIDS. Since 2000, health innovations have cut the number of children who die every year from 10 million to fewer than 5 million."]}),(0,d.jsx)("p",{children:"Of course, innovation can be a double-edged sword. Artificial intelligence can improve education, but it can also eliminate jobs and spread misinformation. Advances in biology make it easier f